  "rationale": "The target is an OR of vaultRead, shareMount, dbReplica and codeRepo. Blocking kerberoast:credentialAccess (whose only parent is wifiGuest) stops ssoLogin:authenticate, which is an AND. Without ssoLogin, fileServer is unreachable, so secretsManager and vaultRead fall. serviceAccount is also unreachable, so dbReplica and codeRepo fall. shareMount still depends only on backupHost:lateralMovement, which is reachable via dbLogin or browserStore and does not involve ssoLogin. Blocking backupHost cuts that branch. So blocking {kerberoast:credentialAccess, backupHost:lateralMovement} makes the target unreachable. One block is not enough: no single non-foothold step lies on every route, because the shareMount route never passes through ssoLogin or kerberoast."
 },
